From: switch-v8 horizon port
Subject: [PATCH] Skip Sweeper free-space zeroing on executable (code) pages (Horizon W^X)

After patch 0008 fixed the marking-barrier code-page flag writes, a second
W^X fault surfaced at higher heap pressure: Sweeper::ZeroOrDiscardUnusedMemory
memset()s freed regions to zero "to help with OS page compression". For an
executable (code-space) NormalPage that memory is the libnx jit_* code arena's
read-only rx alias, so the memset Data-Aborts (observed: PC in memset, LR in
Sweeper::ZeroOrDiscardUnusedMemory, fault address inside the code arena).

V8 guards this with RwxMemoryWriteScope when page->is_executable(), but that
scope is a no-op on Horizon (we cannot re-protect these aliases; code writes go
through the rw alias instead, see patch 0003). The zeroing/discard is purely an
OS-page-compression optimization (v8_flags.zero_unused_memory) and is not
load-bearing for correctness; Horizon has no OS page compression and the
DiscardSystemPages call is already a madvise no-op in the Horizon mman. So skip
the whole routine for executable pages on Horizon. Non-executable data pages are
unaffected.
diff --git a/src/heap/sweeper.cc b/src/heap/sweeper.cc
index 0982c54e..12d6af59 100644
--- a/src/heap/sweeper.cc
+++ b/src/heap/sweeper.cc
@@ -1038,6 +1038,19 @@ void Sweeper::ZeroOrDiscardUnusedMemory(NormalPage* page, Address addr,
     return;
   }
 
+#if V8_OS_HORIZON
+  // Horizon W^X: executable pages live in the libnx jit_* code arena and are
+  // addressed via the read-only rx alias; the memset() zeroing below would
+  // fault (Data Abort) on that alias. The RwxMemoryWriteScope used elsewhere is
+  // a no-op on Horizon (we cannot re-protect; writes use the rw alias instead).
+  // This zeroing is purely an OS-page-compression optimization (see comments
+  // below) and Horizon has no OS page compression, so skip it entirely for
+  // executable pages. (Non-executable data pages fall through unchanged.)
+  if (page->is_executable()) {
+    return;
+  }
+#endif
+
   const Address unused_start = addr + sizeof(FreeSpace);
   DCHECK(page->ContainsLimit(unused_start));
   const Address unused_end = addr + size;
